WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.090
A water molecule and a methane
molecule have almost the same mass.

2
00:00:05.140 --> 00:00:09.250
Methane boils at minus
162 degrees Celsius.

3
00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:11.370
Water boils at 100.

4
00:00:11.420 --> 00:00:17.930
That's a gap of more than 260 degrees between
two molecules of almost the same mass.

5
00:00:17.980 --> 00:00:20.650
Why does water boil so much higher?

6
00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:23.470
In this mission, you'll find
out which bonds are polar,

7
00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:25.310
and which whole molecules are.

8
00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:29.490
You'll meet the forces that act
between molecules, rank them,

9
00:00:29.540 --> 00:00:33.210
and use them to separate
substances by chromatography.

10
00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:37.640
Your mission: explain why water
boils so much higher than methane.
